1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,405
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,407 --> 00:00:02,937
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,076 --> 00:00:05,076
(Episode 19)

4
00:00:06,556 --> 00:00:09,008
So you want to get tested first?

5
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:12,440
It has to be completely secret.

6
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:16,042
- Especially if my mom finds out...
- She'd never approve.

7
00:00:17,312 --> 00:00:20,129
Normally, if you're found to be a match,
we should notify them right away.

8
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:23,583
But I'll ask the center
and see what I can do.

9
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:24,720
Okay.

10
00:00:26,072 --> 00:00:27,546
Are things still tense
between you and your mom?

11
00:00:29,664 --> 00:00:30,848
No.

12
00:00:31,548 --> 00:00:35,028
Things got much better
after dad passed away.

13
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:36,908
You should be good to your mom.

14
00:00:37,652 --> 00:00:40,837
When you got into trouble in high school
and were brought to the hospital,

15
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:44,300
- your mom slapped your dad.
- What?

16
00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:47,657
It was because your dad
didn't handle things properly.

17
00:00:48,810 --> 00:00:53,051
You have no idea
how much Se Ri cried back then.

18
00:00:53,910 --> 00:00:56,370
If you'd seen your mom back then,

19
00:00:56,371 --> 00:00:58,331
you wouldn't be able
to fight with her now.

20
00:00:59,903 --> 00:01:01,475
That's what parents are like.

21
00:01:05,112 --> 00:01:06,284
Yes.

22
00:01:06,388 --> 00:01:07,953
Are you really
going through with the bone marrow test?

23
00:01:08,506 --> 00:01:10,062
Are you absolutely sure?

24
00:01:10,712 --> 00:01:12,972
Of course, we'll only know after the test,

25
00:01:13,216 --> 00:01:17,084
but if you're a match,
it'll be hard not to donate.

26
00:01:17,190 --> 00:01:18,954
Think about your decision one more time...

27
00:01:18,955 --> 00:01:21,343
I'll only think about that child.

28
00:01:23,070 --> 00:01:25,971
That child made my dad smile
one last time.

29
00:01:26,504 --> 00:01:29,848
Everyone had so much to say
about dad's death,

30
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:33,011
but that child and I couldn't say a word.

31
00:01:34,472 --> 00:01:35,712
Sir,

32
00:01:36,644 --> 00:01:40,269
I feel like that child is just like me.

33
00:01:42,692 --> 00:01:44,762
Okay. I understand.

34
00:01:44,976 --> 00:01:47,741
- I'll schedule it and call you.
- Okay.

35
00:01:50,170 --> 00:01:52,678
Most importantly, please make sure...

36
00:01:52,679 --> 00:01:54,048
I got it, kid.

37
00:01:54,288 --> 00:01:56,248
I'll keep it completely anonymous.

38
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:59,773
For non-family donors,
anonymity is the rule.

39
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:01,784
There's nothing to worry about.

40
00:02:01,785 --> 00:02:04,016
Okay. Please call me, then.

41
00:02:04,548 --> 00:02:06,725
My lunch break is almost over.

42
00:02:06,726 --> 00:02:07,726
Okay.

43
00:02:33,644 --> 00:02:36,465
- What brings you here?
- My child is sick.

44
00:02:36,896 --> 00:02:38,166
Why are you here?

45
00:02:39,776 --> 00:02:41,232
I saw Seung Woo here too.

46
00:02:41,612 --> 00:02:43,307
Is someone in your family sick?

47
00:02:43,372 --> 00:02:44,587
You saw him?

48
00:02:45,668 --> 00:02:47,317
He looked like he'd lost a lot of weight.

49
00:02:49,472 --> 00:02:50,796
Be careful.

50
00:02:51,070 --> 00:02:53,520
My nephew is sick and staying nearby,
so you can't let anyone see you.

51
00:02:53,584 --> 00:02:54,732
Why?

52
00:02:54,930 --> 00:02:57,328
- Can't I see him just once?
- Are you out of your mind?

53
00:02:57,456 --> 00:02:59,791
Are you really trying
to destroy his whole family?

54
00:02:59,796 --> 00:03:01,860
He can't even go to the station now.

55
00:03:01,896 --> 00:03:03,304
I dropped the lawsuit over the affair.

56
00:03:03,352 --> 00:03:06,765
- That got me caught too.
- Enough.

57
00:03:06,810 --> 00:03:10,358
Everything is already at its worst.
We can't have anything else happen.

58
00:03:11,964 --> 00:03:15,794
- Be careful, look after the child...
- Seung Woo.

59
00:03:29,716 --> 00:03:31,388
I had something to tell you anyway.

60
00:03:32,832 --> 00:03:34,488
I missed you.

61
00:03:37,063 --> 00:03:38,887
Can you come to the station tomorrow?

62
00:03:38,888 --> 00:03:39,926
I'll see you tomorrow.

63
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:41,142
Is that okay?

64
00:03:41,730 --> 00:03:43,320
Will you see me?

65
00:03:49,824 --> 00:03:51,081
Hey.

66
00:03:57,452 --> 00:03:58,652
I said I had something to say.

67
00:03:58,716 --> 00:04:01,059
Do you still need to talk to that woman?

68
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:04,684
- That's none of your business.
- Right. I guess it isn't.

69
00:04:06,252 --> 00:04:07,919
Please take the bone marrow test.

70
00:04:10,770 --> 00:04:13,440
- Why should I?
- None of us is a match.

71
00:04:14,010 --> 00:04:16,792
Please do me this favor.
I heard my mom went to see you yesterday.

72
00:04:16,904 --> 00:04:18,154
We're desperate.

73
00:04:19,172 --> 00:04:21,354
- Please help us.
- Just because you ask,

74
00:04:22,110 --> 00:04:23,964
do I have to do everything you want?

75
00:04:24,992 --> 00:04:27,274
I asked for a favor a long time ago too.

76
00:04:28,650 --> 00:04:30,442
What did you do to me then?

77
00:04:34,532 --> 00:04:36,962
- I'm sorry.
- That apology doesn't feel sincere.

78
00:04:36,983 --> 00:04:38,000
Hey.

79
00:04:40,352 --> 00:04:41,462
No.

80
00:04:42,076 --> 00:04:44,987
- I really mean it.
- You mean you really need me.

81
00:04:46,352 --> 00:04:47,421
But back then,

82
00:04:48,748 --> 00:04:51,005
I asked you sincerely too.

83
00:04:51,092 --> 00:04:53,371
I didn't choose to be born,

84
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:56,156
so I came to you begging you to save me.

85
00:04:57,992 --> 00:05:00,144
You said so many cruel things
to me back then.

86
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:02,544
Do you remember?

87
00:05:04,952 --> 00:05:06,129
I'm really...

88
00:05:07,202 --> 00:05:08,568
I'm really sorry.

89
00:05:10,172 --> 00:05:11,810
Seeing how much you cared for O Reum,

90
00:05:12,644 --> 00:05:14,242
how you came over and played with him,

91
00:05:14,724 --> 00:05:16,664
and how attached he became to you...

92
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:19,141
made me reflect on myself.

93
00:05:20,432 --> 00:05:22,669
You're a better person than I am.

94
00:05:23,544 --> 00:05:24,733
Thanks.

95
00:05:26,970 --> 00:05:28,554
I'll think about it.

96
00:06:10,204 --> 00:06:11,462
Yeong Ju.

97
00:06:15,436 --> 00:06:17,867
I heard you took the bone marrow test.

98
00:06:18,288 --> 00:06:19,578
Thank you.

99
00:06:20,492 --> 00:06:22,655
It was the least I could do.

100
00:06:25,830 --> 00:06:28,028
Aren't you going to fix this house?

101
00:06:31,772 --> 00:06:33,301
I've got a lot of gray hair too, right?

102
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,420
I'm getting old.

103
00:06:37,676 --> 00:06:39,064
Well, yeah.

104
00:06:39,432 --> 00:06:41,824
You can't stay full of energy forever.

105
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,740
Where's all that fire from back when...

106
00:06:46,168 --> 00:06:49,148
you came at their dad with a knife?

107
00:06:49,230 --> 00:06:51,714
I still regret not killing him back then.

108
00:06:54,512 --> 00:06:56,196
When I heard he died,

109
00:06:56,436 --> 00:06:58,419
I happened to have business
at that hospital,

110
00:06:59,556 --> 00:07:01,495
but I couldn't go into the funeral hall.

111
00:07:01,532 --> 00:07:02,632
I'm sorry.

112
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:04,376
It's better you didn't come.

113
00:07:04,432 --> 00:07:05,871
I heard there were
two separate funeral rooms.

114
00:07:05,873 --> 00:07:09,717
That crazy bitch. She stabbed you
in the heart till the very end.

115
00:07:09,872 --> 00:07:12,684
- Someday, I swear I'll...
- Hey!

116
00:07:13,012 --> 00:07:15,208
Don't say stuff like that.
I don't want to hear it.

117
00:07:15,270 --> 00:07:17,608
This is why I call you an idiot.

118
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:20,035
- Why can't you just cut them off?
- Forget it.

119
00:07:21,092 --> 00:07:24,062
I was going to thank you anyway.
You came at the perfect time.

120
00:07:24,064 --> 00:07:25,404
Let's stop here.

121
00:07:26,672 --> 00:07:28,785
If we keep talking,
it's not going to end well between us.

122
00:07:28,788 --> 00:07:31,241
- You know that, right?
- I know.

123
00:07:36,264 --> 00:07:38,671
Use this for the hospital bills.
It's not much.

124
00:07:41,432 --> 00:07:43,635
It's okay. Go buy yourself a suit.

125
00:07:46,352 --> 00:07:49,198
You're kind of an idiot,
but you have such a good heart.

126
00:07:49,199 --> 00:07:50,996
Why is your luck so terrible?

127
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:57,017
Take care of yourself.

128
00:08:20,899 --> 00:08:21,899
(Dr. Hwang)

129
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:29,885
- Yes, sir?
- Ji Ni,

130
00:08:30,632 --> 00:08:32,829
you're a match for...

131
00:08:33,719 --> 00:08:36,417
- O Reum's bone marrow.
- Really?

132
00:08:37,084 --> 00:08:39,219
Ji Ni, let's go get ice cream.

133
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:42,664
- Who is that?
- What?

134
00:08:44,243 --> 00:08:46,221
Yes. I understand.

135
00:08:48,272 --> 00:08:50,019
It was a work call.

136
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:52,585
What did you say, Mom?

137
00:08:53,556 --> 00:08:55,659
- That's weird.
- Why?

138
00:08:56,740 --> 00:08:57,904
What is it?

139
00:09:04,470 --> 00:09:06,180
You're hiding something, aren't you?

140
00:09:06,676 --> 00:09:08,579
Did something happen to that kid?

141
00:09:08,730 --> 00:09:11,745
- Give me your phone.
- No, really.

142
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:14,588
Tae O suggested a summer workshop.

143
00:09:14,708 --> 00:09:18,282
I was just asking if it's okay
to go right after getting hired.

144
00:09:18,392 --> 00:09:20,615
- Really?
- Really.

145
00:09:20,970 --> 00:09:23,250
Mom, what's with you?
I'm not a little kid anymore.

146
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:25,514
You're not a little kid anymore,
that's exactly why.

147
00:09:27,168 --> 00:09:29,670
- Come on, let's go get ice cream.
- I don't want any.

148
00:09:33,630 --> 00:09:35,173
Dictator.

149
00:09:39,024 --> 00:09:42,628
You're not going alone with Tae O.
I don't care if it's for work.

150
00:09:42,630 --> 00:09:44,194
Then I'm coming with you.

151
00:09:44,196 --> 00:09:47,217
I was actually just asking Jung A
if she wanted to come along.

152
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:48,932
What am I, an elementary school kid?

153
00:09:48,952 --> 00:09:50,863
When I was a kid, you let dad go alone.

154
00:09:53,610 --> 00:09:57,528
- Did I do that on purpose?
- Okay, fine. I said it wrong.

155
00:09:58,564 --> 00:10:00,554
I'll talk it over
and let you know what we decide.

156
00:10:01,872 --> 00:10:05,467
Once the money comes in from Indonesia,
we can expand the business...

157
00:10:12,424 --> 00:10:15,205
My business cards are ready. Nice, right?

158
00:10:18,914 --> 00:10:22,031
If you told me,
I could've designed them for you.

159
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:23,574
I should've asked you.

160
00:10:23,576 --> 00:10:25,864
I just used the template your dad made
and added my name.

161
00:10:25,872 --> 00:10:28,242
- Next time, you do it.
- Okay.

162
00:10:34,110 --> 00:10:37,172
Just the two of us like this,
it's not so bad, right?

163
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:55,596
Ji Ni, you're a match
for O Reum's bone marrow.

164
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:07,670
Hi, it's me.

165
00:11:09,052 --> 00:11:11,181
I'm not feeling well today,

166
00:11:11,190 --> 00:11:13,392
so I'll stop by the hospital
before heading to work.

167
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:16,892
I'm really sorry.

168
00:11:16,948 --> 00:11:19,319
I only just started.

169
00:11:20,557 --> 00:11:21,821
Yes.

170
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:24,573
I understand.

171
00:11:48,469 --> 00:11:49,846
(The Late Cha Min Ki)

172
00:11:54,624 --> 00:11:57,628
Dad, it's me.
I came because I'm so conflicted.

173
00:11:58,112 --> 00:11:59,368
Tell me.

174
00:11:59,370 --> 00:12:01,078
What should I do?

175
00:12:02,850 --> 00:12:04,658
Can I just follow my heart?

176
00:12:05,430 --> 00:12:07,269
Will mom understand?

177
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:10,947
They're the people who destroyed her.

178
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:15,728
Is it okay for me to help them?

179
00:12:16,692 --> 00:12:20,890
My parents worked so hard
to buy this house.

180
00:12:21,092 --> 00:12:22,652
What right do you have to do this?

181
00:12:22,876 --> 00:12:24,596
"What right?"

182
00:12:25,172 --> 00:12:27,940
The man who worked so hard to buy it...

183
00:12:28,284 --> 00:12:29,460
is my father-in-law.

184
00:12:29,544 --> 00:12:33,790
- You really want to do this?
- Mom!

185
00:12:35,024 --> 00:12:36,337
Don't touch her!

186
00:12:37,028 --> 00:12:38,758
I'm so disappointed in you.

187
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:42,180
A homewrecker's property
isn't protected by law.

188
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:44,025
A homewrecker...

189
00:12:44,432 --> 00:12:46,547
has no legal protection.

190
00:13:31,248 --> 00:13:33,305
I want to go home.

191
00:13:36,071 --> 00:13:37,116
O Reum...

192
00:13:37,117 --> 00:13:40,793
They say I can't yet. I hate it here.

193
00:13:42,404 --> 00:13:46,627
I hope you get better soon.

194
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:48,260
Will you come again?

195
00:13:56,688 --> 00:13:59,588
- Hello.
- Are you sick? Are you at the hospital?

196
00:14:00,024 --> 00:14:01,228
No.

197
00:14:03,248 --> 00:14:04,887
I came to see dad.

198
00:14:07,941 --> 00:14:11,274
Jung A, I'm so conflicted.

199
00:14:11,275 --> 00:14:12,569
Why? What is it?

200
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:18,059
Really? Your bone marrow is a match?

201
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:19,581
Yes.

202
00:14:20,049 --> 00:14:23,104
I think it would've been easier
if it hadn't matched,

203
00:14:23,417 --> 00:14:24,732
but that's not what I want.

204
00:14:24,733 --> 00:14:27,875
I want that child to grow up healthy.

205
00:14:29,275 --> 00:14:31,857
If only we weren't related at all.

206
00:14:31,858 --> 00:14:34,440
I would've rushed over
and donated my bone marrow.

207
00:14:34,441 --> 00:14:37,066
Then it would've been easier
to tell mom too.

208
00:14:37,108 --> 00:14:38,847
You're truly kind.

209
00:14:38,983 --> 00:14:40,447
I don't think I could do it.

210
00:14:41,066 --> 00:14:43,935
It was because
your dad didn't handle things properly.

211
00:14:44,483 --> 00:14:46,483
He's absolutely adorable.

212
00:14:46,525 --> 00:14:48,766
He's the son of the woman
who tried to take your house.

213
00:14:49,483 --> 00:14:51,536
That's just between the adults.

214
00:14:51,733 --> 00:14:53,332
So the problem is your mom?

215
00:14:54,775 --> 00:14:56,220
Do you think she'll feel betrayed?

216
00:14:56,483 --> 00:14:58,441
Knowing my mom,
she'll try to kill me, right?

217
00:14:58,483 --> 00:15:01,191
No. She'll probably try to kill herself.

218
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:04,107
If I were her,
I couldn't forgive a daughter like you.

219
00:15:04,108 --> 00:15:07,412
Not you too. Don't say that.

220
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:10,178
I'll give you my honest opinion.

221
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:11,400
Do you want to hear it?

222
00:15:13,650 --> 00:15:16,077
They have to pay for being so shameless.

223
00:15:16,441 --> 00:15:19,149
I can't forgive them either
for coming to your house.

224
00:15:19,150 --> 00:15:20,690
No matter what the law says,

225
00:15:20,691 --> 00:15:23,366
how could they claim a house
they didn't pay a cent for?

226
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:26,311
Wait. Let me finish.

227
00:15:27,179 --> 00:15:29,357
If they end up losing O Reum,

228
00:15:29,358 --> 00:15:31,650
tell them to have another child
and raise it while living right.

229
00:15:31,691 --> 00:15:33,316
And you take your mom's side.

230
00:15:33,608 --> 00:15:35,107
Your mom has only you now.

231
00:15:35,108 --> 00:15:36,424
If you betray her,

232
00:15:36,816 --> 00:15:38,856
you'll be Judas, you know?

233
00:15:38,858 --> 00:15:40,868
Judas Iscariot, the symbol of betrayal.

234
00:15:42,441 --> 00:15:45,733
Whatever family connection
O Reum and I have,

235
00:15:45,775 --> 00:15:49,416
none of that matters.
I just want to save him.

236
00:15:49,691 --> 00:15:52,025
Just like I wanted to live.

237
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:56,274
I can save him despite his parents,

238
00:15:56,275 --> 00:15:59,377
so I don't understand why those parents
are the reason I can't.

239
00:15:59,858 --> 00:16:02,608
O Reum must feel as wronged as I did.

240
00:16:02,691 --> 00:16:05,650
I understand what you mean,
but listen to me.

241
00:16:06,025 --> 00:16:07,203
You can't do this.

242
00:16:07,259 --> 00:16:09,181
It would break your mom's heart again.

243
00:16:15,858 --> 00:16:16,858
O Reum.

244
00:16:17,816 --> 00:16:19,921
Want to share some mango with me?

245
00:16:20,451 --> 00:16:23,431
You ate a lot of this
at your grandpa's house.

246
00:16:23,608 --> 00:16:24,743
Remember?

247
00:16:26,011 --> 00:16:27,690
I remember.

248
00:16:27,691 --> 00:16:31,150
You ate so much,
your grandpa was surprised.

249
00:16:31,191 --> 00:16:34,357
Right. This isn't mango.

250
00:16:34,359 --> 00:16:36,484
This is mango too.

251
00:16:36,691 --> 00:16:38,021
It tastes just the same.

252
00:16:38,022 --> 00:16:40,858
No. That's not it.

253
00:16:41,066 --> 00:16:43,019
They said you have to eat this for now.

254
00:16:43,566 --> 00:16:46,025
When you get better,
we'll go have real mango.

255
00:16:46,150 --> 00:16:48,635
I'll take you there. I promise.

256
00:16:55,650 --> 00:16:57,899
It's not bad, right?

257
00:16:57,900 --> 00:17:00,650
- Bongao.
- Bongao?

258
00:17:01,326 --> 00:17:02,920
Bongao. Here.

259
00:17:05,608 --> 00:17:06,608
Is that okay?

260
00:17:07,483 --> 00:17:10,566
Dried or sterilized food is okay.

261
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:13,275
I miss the drawing lady.

262
00:17:13,566 --> 00:17:16,241
She's busy. She got a job at a company.

263
00:17:16,691 --> 00:17:18,233
Here, let's have one more bite.

264
00:17:44,641 --> 00:17:47,729
You had the affair lawsuit withdrawn.
Thank you.

265
00:17:48,108 --> 00:17:49,185
I'm sorry.

266
00:17:50,108 --> 00:17:51,274
Did you actually love me?

267
00:17:51,275 --> 00:17:52,816
Does that matter?

268
00:17:54,691 --> 00:17:55,763
Right. I guess not.

269
00:17:57,275 --> 00:17:58,275
I did.

270
00:17:59,885 --> 00:18:02,770
More than I ever thought
I could love someone.

271
00:18:04,650 --> 00:18:06,793
But I can't run away with you.

272
00:18:12,149 --> 00:18:13,890
Then that wasn't love.

273
00:18:14,063 --> 00:18:16,314
The most important person
in my life is me.

274
00:18:16,383 --> 00:18:18,242
No one is more important than me.

275
00:18:20,066 --> 00:18:23,183
Thanks for being honest. Goodbye.

276
00:18:25,066 --> 00:18:26,281
Seung Woo.

277
00:18:27,025 --> 00:18:30,454
If I get divorced and come back to you,
will you take me back?

278
00:18:32,719 --> 00:18:34,962
- Are you serious?
- Do I sound like I'm lying?

279
00:18:39,899 --> 00:18:42,981
If you come back after your divorce,
I'll take you back.

280
00:18:42,983 --> 00:18:44,637
If you leave everything behind.

281
00:18:47,108 --> 00:18:50,558
But you won't do that.

282
00:18:51,246 --> 00:18:54,496
As you said, you're the one
who matters most in your life.

283
00:18:54,733 --> 00:18:57,482
You don't even know what sincerity means.

284
00:18:57,638 --> 00:18:59,572
What you call love...

285
00:19:00,316 --> 00:19:02,047
is nothing but a matchstick...

286
00:19:02,733 --> 00:19:04,614
that flares up for a moment.

287
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:12,613
I'm telling you
because you don't seem to know yourself.

288
00:19:24,316 --> 00:19:25,962
I heard you met her again.

289
00:19:28,066 --> 00:19:29,650
(Letter of Resignation)

290
00:19:31,160 --> 00:19:32,899
Thank you for everything.

291
00:19:32,955 --> 00:19:33,996
Will you meet her again?

292
00:19:34,025 --> 00:19:35,345
What is this...

293
00:19:35,680 --> 00:19:37,857
some boys' school that bans dating?

294
00:19:37,858 --> 00:19:39,411
Why are you so fixated on it?

295
00:19:39,650 --> 00:19:41,034
I already resigned.

296
00:19:41,275 --> 00:19:44,734
Hey, if you take a little more time
to reflect on yourself...

297
00:19:44,736 --> 00:19:45,854
Sir.

298
00:19:45,855 --> 00:19:47,731
Like they say in the movies,

299
00:19:47,888 --> 00:19:50,025
I may be short on money, but not on pride.

300
00:19:50,155 --> 00:19:52,519
And I'm good at what I do.

301
00:19:52,858 --> 00:19:55,316
Having an affair
doesn't make me incompetent,

302
00:19:55,358 --> 00:19:58,400
so I'll find a place
where I can work even harder.

303
00:19:58,474 --> 00:19:59,799
Don't worry too much.

304
00:20:00,733 --> 00:20:02,177
That confidence of yours...

305
00:20:04,483 --> 00:20:05,831
Okay. I understand.

306
00:20:07,483 --> 00:20:11,517
Give this to your mother.

307
00:20:11,540 --> 00:20:14,747
I heard the child is sick.
It's not much, but it's from me.

308
00:20:17,191 --> 00:20:19,232
With everything going on,
and now you too...

309
00:20:19,233 --> 00:20:21,210
Yeong Ju must feel terrible.

310
00:20:21,933 --> 00:20:24,016
Yes. All I can say is I'm sorry.

311
00:20:24,108 --> 00:20:27,100
You punk. Keep your eyes open next time.

312
00:20:27,483 --> 00:20:29,755
Yes, I'll keep my eyes open.

313
00:20:30,566 --> 00:20:31,732
I'll pass it along.

314
00:20:31,733 --> 00:20:35,691
Okay. Let's have a drink sometime.

315
00:20:36,275 --> 00:20:37,275
Okay.

316
00:21:17,255 --> 00:21:18,607
So you're unemployed now?

317
00:21:18,608 --> 00:21:20,011
Just for a while.

318
00:21:20,289 --> 00:21:22,982
Seriously, just for a bit. Trust me, Mom.

319
00:21:22,983 --> 00:21:24,316
I've got what it takes.

320
00:21:24,803 --> 00:21:29,714
I'll land something better soon.
You'll see.

321
00:21:36,383 --> 00:21:39,358
At this rate,
you're going to turn into an alcoholic.

322
00:21:40,733 --> 00:21:43,650
Then just throw me into rehab.

323
00:21:43,941 --> 00:21:45,709
How can you say that?

324
00:21:46,691 --> 00:21:48,983
I need some hope to keep going.

325
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:51,816
That woman ruined you like this
and she's probably living just fine.

326
00:21:51,858 --> 00:21:54,703
I need to drag her by the hair
just so I can breathe again.

327
00:21:54,775 --> 00:21:58,280
Don't. She's pitiful.

328
00:21:58,983 --> 00:22:00,017
What?

329
00:22:01,525 --> 00:22:05,233
- Seriously, you...
- Yeong Ju.

330
00:22:05,608 --> 00:22:08,715
If someone treats love like a joke,
isn't that pitiful?

331
00:22:09,566 --> 00:22:10,837
I'm sorry.

332
00:22:11,191 --> 00:22:12,400
I'm sorry.

333
00:22:13,900 --> 00:22:16,660
I'm sorry for disappointing you.

334
00:22:17,441 --> 00:22:20,315
- I'm really sorry.
- What will you do now?

335
00:22:20,316 --> 00:22:23,737
If you lose your job too,
how are you supposed to live?

336
00:22:27,191 --> 00:22:30,753
It's okay.
Someone like me has plenty of options.

337
00:22:30,858 --> 00:22:33,175
Find a new job within a month.

338
00:22:33,983 --> 00:22:35,689
If not, I'll kick you out.

339
00:22:35,691 --> 00:22:36,978
I can't even stand looking at you.

340
00:22:37,525 --> 00:22:38,833
A month?

341
00:22:39,691 --> 00:22:42,808
Don't worry. I'll do it in ten days.

342
00:22:44,150 --> 00:22:46,232
Yeong Ju, don't you trust me?

343
00:22:46,233 --> 00:22:47,439
Should I?

344
00:22:48,483 --> 00:22:50,449
You can't even judge people properly.

345
00:22:52,441 --> 00:22:56,215
Yeah, guess I got that from you.

346
00:22:58,108 --> 00:22:59,185
You...

347
00:23:31,025 --> 00:23:32,483
(My Beloved Pain in the Neck 1)

348
00:23:35,721 --> 00:23:37,010
Hey, Seung Hyun.

349
00:23:38,869 --> 00:23:42,141
What? The ICU?

350
00:23:43,899 --> 00:23:45,451
You look great, Na Se Ri.

351
00:23:45,453 --> 00:23:48,233
You've really got that model vibe now.

352
00:23:48,566 --> 00:23:50,169
A model? Please.

353
00:23:51,566 --> 00:23:55,553
Actually, my investment
in Indonesian TV paid off.

354
00:23:56,783 --> 00:23:59,494
Guess my husband set it up
for Ji Ni and me.

355
00:23:59,608 --> 00:24:03,191
He was a romantic to the end. I'm jealous.

356
00:24:03,599 --> 00:24:06,058
My husband's just a big old drunk.

357
00:24:07,191 --> 00:24:10,613
Hey, growing old together
as a couple is something to envy.

358
00:24:11,066 --> 00:24:13,066
I still miss my husband.

359
00:24:13,150 --> 00:24:15,553
She's always been devoted to her marriage.

360
00:24:16,441 --> 00:24:19,786
That looks like more
than devotion, though.

361
00:24:20,900 --> 00:24:23,325
Honestly, I do feel a sense of freedom.

362
00:24:24,168 --> 00:24:27,801
Since he was never completely mine,

363
00:24:28,150 --> 00:24:30,900
I was always on edge, always watching.

364
00:24:31,025 --> 00:24:33,358
In that sense, it's easier now.

365
00:24:33,858 --> 00:24:35,123
That sounds strange, right?

366
00:24:35,233 --> 00:24:37,773
I thought you'd struggle a lot longer.

367
00:24:37,925 --> 00:24:39,649
I heard you lost all your students too.

368
00:24:40,733 --> 00:24:42,023
It's not like it didn't hit me,

369
00:24:42,025 --> 00:24:43,816
but I still have to live.

370
00:24:46,811 --> 00:24:48,066
Sa Bin. Don't go.

371
00:24:48,150 --> 00:24:50,566
It's okay, come in.

372
00:24:52,316 --> 00:24:53,990
These are my arts high school friends.

373
00:24:54,109 --> 00:24:55,931
You know him, right? My number one fan.

374
00:24:55,933 --> 00:24:58,858
Of course. You're Clara and Brahms.

375
00:24:59,316 --> 00:25:00,525
Are you two still the same?

376
00:25:01,025 --> 00:25:02,233
Yes.

377
00:25:03,444 --> 00:25:05,566
You guys should go,
You said you had plans.

378
00:25:05,983 --> 00:25:08,941
Yeah. Sa Bin, let's meet again next time.

379
00:25:09,025 --> 00:25:10,763
Sure, take care.

380
00:25:10,858 --> 00:25:12,233
I'll walk you out.

381
00:25:23,315 --> 00:25:25,940
(CEO Na Se Ri)

382
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:34,233
Sa Bin, you're not upset, right?

383
00:25:34,316 --> 00:25:35,858
I'm fine.

384
00:25:36,691 --> 00:25:39,691
Do you play the cello here?

385
00:25:40,025 --> 00:25:41,963
I'm planning to sell it.

386
00:25:41,964 --> 00:25:44,024
I don't teach cello anymore anyway.

387
00:25:44,066 --> 00:25:45,441
No point in keeping so many.

388
00:25:45,734 --> 00:25:47,608
I'm clearing things out
to help with expenses.

389
00:25:47,650 --> 00:25:49,316
How much is it?

390
00:25:49,733 --> 00:25:52,025
- You want to buy it?
- Is it expensive?

391
00:25:52,108 --> 00:25:55,412
Instead of your cello going to a stranger,

392
00:25:55,441 --> 00:25:56,856
I'd rather be the one who keeps it.

393
00:25:57,156 --> 00:26:00,108
Should I try learning cello too?

394
00:26:00,150 --> 00:26:01,607
Do you think I could?

395
00:26:01,685 --> 00:26:03,299
I'm actually tone-deaf.

396
00:26:03,372 --> 00:26:05,562
Would I be better at this than singing?

397
00:26:06,816 --> 00:26:09,128
Why are you being so nice?
You're making my heart flutter.

398
00:26:09,191 --> 00:26:10,441
I'm your Brahms, after all.

399
00:26:10,525 --> 00:26:12,585
I just wanted to help.

400
00:26:13,483 --> 00:26:15,941
I know, you always look out for me.

401
00:26:16,405 --> 00:26:17,480
Want something to drink?

402
00:26:18,203 --> 00:26:20,774
This is herbal tonic.

403
00:26:20,775 --> 00:26:22,524
The summer really drains your energy.

404
00:26:22,525 --> 00:26:24,681
You must be exhausted
starting a new business.

405
00:26:25,025 --> 00:26:26,691
Drink this and get your strength back.

406
00:26:29,330 --> 00:26:30,420
Sa Bin,

407
00:26:30,421 --> 00:26:33,552
what do you think would've happened
if we'd met at twenty?

408
00:26:34,275 --> 00:26:37,362
I'd probably be completely swept up
in your charm,

409
00:26:37,363 --> 00:26:38,691
like I am now.

410
00:26:38,733 --> 00:26:39,939
What?

411
00:26:41,191 --> 00:26:45,313
With lines like that,
why are you still single?

412
00:26:45,452 --> 00:26:47,411
Not that I mind.

413
00:26:51,150 --> 00:26:53,393
O Reum.

414
00:26:54,066 --> 00:26:56,349
- O Reum.
- O Reum.

415
00:26:56,400 --> 00:26:58,767
O Reum.

416
00:27:01,441 --> 00:27:02,650
Are you okay?

417
00:27:03,025 --> 00:27:04,233
O Reum.

418
00:27:05,816 --> 00:27:07,400
O Reum.

419
00:27:57,275 --> 00:28:00,483
(Family Register)

420
00:28:00,525 --> 00:28:01,857
No. Absolutely not.

421
00:28:01,858 --> 00:28:03,149
Please at least let her get tested.

422
00:28:03,150 --> 00:28:05,899
If she's a match,
you'll all start taking turns coming here.

423
00:28:05,900 --> 00:28:07,733
So now you want my daughter's bone marrow?

424
00:28:07,763 --> 00:28:09,304
She said if mom came and apologized,

425
00:28:09,358 --> 00:28:11,065
she'd reconsider, right?

426
00:28:11,066 --> 00:28:13,064
- Get a grip.
- Does that even make sense?

427
00:28:13,066 --> 00:28:14,733
Do you want me to do it?

428
00:28:14,775 --> 00:28:16,275
Are there no side effects?

429
00:28:16,316 --> 00:28:17,607
Will your body be okay?

430
00:28:17,608 --> 00:28:20,900
Ms. Na Ji Ni, is this admirable
or reckless?

431
00:28:22,273 --> 00:28:24,273
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
